# Local env files
#
# dotenvx convention (copied from final-hill/cathedral): the encrypted
# `.env.<env>` files ARE committed — they are ciphertext, safe to publish — while
# `.env.keys` holds the private keys and must never be. Ignoring `.env.*` wholesale
# (the previous rule) made the committed-ciphertext model impossible.
#
# Order matters: ignore first, then re-include the specific files. Git cannot
# re-include a path whose parent directory is excluded, but these are files.
.env
.env.*
.env.keys
!.env
!.env.local
!.env.production
!.env.example

# preview helper
.output/preview-root

# Import bookkeeping (source revision, batch size) — regenerated on each run
scripts/.pldb-import.json
